<% content_for :stylesheets, area_stylesheet_link_tags("workbench") %>
<% content_for :title, t("briefing.tools.comparison") %>
<% chart = Rails.configuration.x.oaci_chart %>
<section class="dev-tools dev-console dev-comparison" data-controller="comparison"
         data-comparison-tiles-value="<%= chart.tiles %>"
         data-comparison-attribution-value="<%= chart.attribution %>">
  <h1>Traffic comparison <span>&middot; a SoftRF Retro Mk&nbsp;II over USB beside a skyBlip&nbsp;Bravo over Bluetooth</span></h1>

  <div class="layout">
    <%= render "source", source: "retro", name: "SoftRF Retro Mk II", transport: "serial" %>
    <%= render "source", source: "bravo", name: "skyBlip Bravo", transport: "bluetooth" %>

    <div class="panel panel-chart">
      <h2>Chart</h2>
      <div class="bar">
        <button type="button" data-action="comparison#zoomOut" aria-label="Zoom out">&minus;</button>
        <button type="button" data-action="comparison#zoomIn" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
        <span class="state" data-comparison-target="chartState">-</span>
      </div>
      <canvas class="chart" data-comparison-target="chart" data-action="click->comparison#pick"
              aria-label="Traffic from both receivers on the OACI chart, pick an aircraft to compare it" role="img"></canvas>
      <form class="row" data-action="comparison#saveChart">
        <label class="check">Latitude <input type="number" name="latitude" step="any" value="<%= chart.centre[:latitude] %>" required></label>
        <label class="check">Longitude <input type="number" name="longitude" step="any" value="<%= chart.centre[:longitude] %>" required></label>
        <label class="check">Radius, km <input type="number" name="radius" min="10" max="300" value="<%= chart.radius_km %>" required></label>
        <button type="submit">Save the chart offline</button>
        <span class="state" data-comparison-target="saveState"></span>
      </form>
      <div class="hint">The chart centres on the receiver that has a fix, and on the saved area before that.
        Save the area before the flight, and open the page before takeoff: tiles come from IGN's Géoplateforme and stay in this browser, the page does not.
        <span class="chart-key chart-key-retro">Retro</span> <span class="chart-key chart-key-bravo">Bravo</span>
        draw the same aircraft joined by a dashed line, with the height above us in hundreds of feet. Pick one to compare it.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel panel-focus">
      <h2>Selected aircraft</h2>
      <p class="state" data-comparison-target="focusEmpty">Pick an aircraft on the chart or in the table below.</p>
      <div data-comparison-target="focusBody" hidden>
        <p class="focus-title" data-comparison-target="focusTitle"></p>
        <p class="state" data-comparison-target="focusSummary"></p>
        <canvas class="timeline" data-comparison-target="timeline" role="img"
                aria-label="The seconds each receiver listed the aircraft, its distance and its signal level"></canvas>
        <div class="hint">A lane marks each second a receiver listed the aircraft, and a tall mark a new position, which only GDL&nbsp;90 tells apart.
          Below the lanes: distance, then RSSI when a receiver sends one.</div>
        <div class="traffic-scroll">
          <table class="traffic focus-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col" class="chart-key-retro">Retro</th><th scope="col" class="chart-key-bravo">Bravo</th><th scope="col">Retro &minus; Bravo</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody data-comparison-target="focusRows"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="bar"><button type="button" data-action="comparison#unfocus">Clear the selection</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel panel-wide">
      <h2>Aircraft</h2>
      <p class="state" data-comparison-target="tally">-</p>
      <div class="traffic-scroll">
        <table class="traffic">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th rowspan="2" scope="col">Address</th>
              <th rowspan="2" scope="col">Callsign</th>
              <th rowspan="2" scope="col">Heard by</th>
              <th rowspan="2" scope="col">First</th>
              <th colspan="7" scope="colgroup" class="chart-key-retro">Retro</th>
              <th colspan="7" scope="colgroup" class="chart-key-bravo">Bravo</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <% 2.times do %>
                <th scope="col">Age, s</th><th scope="col">Dist, km</th><th scope="col">Rel, ft</th><th scope="col">Listed</th>
                <th scope="col">Drops</th><th scope="col">New/min</th><th scope="col">RSSI</th>
              <% end %>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody data-comparison-target="aircraft"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="hint">Listed is the share of the seconds either receiver listed the aircraft, and a drop a gap of more than 3&nbsp;s.
        New/min counts new positions, which only GDL&nbsp;90 tells apart: NMEA repeats or dead-reckons a target between messages.
        RSSI shows when a receiver's <code>$PFLAA</code> carries one: SoftRF on the Retro's STM32 sends none, in GDL&nbsp;90 or NMEA.
        Distances and heights come from the Bravo's fix and pressure altitude, and from the Retro's own when the Bravo has none.</div>
    </div>

    <% { "retro" => "Retro", "bravo" => "Bravo" }.each do |source, label| %>
      <div class="panel panel-wide">
        <h2><%= label %>: every attribute decoded</h2>
        <div class="traffic-scroll">
          <table class="traffic" data-comparison-target="attributes" data-source="<%= source %>"></table>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <div class="panel panel-wide">
      <h2>Why the two lists differ</h2>
      <div class="hint">The Retro speaks GDL&nbsp;90 by default and the Bravo FLARM NMEA, so each list shows its protocol's fields.
        GDL&nbsp;90 sends an absolute position, the pressure altitude, the position's integrity and accuracy (NIC, NACp) and the ADS-B emitter category.
        <code>$PFLAA</code> sends a position relative to the receiver's own fix, a FLARM aircraft type, and on a skyBlip the source.
        Set the Retro to NMEA to read <code>$PFLAA</code> on both sides, without the Retro's RSSI.
        SoftRF also leaves out of GDL&nbsp;90 an aircraft farther than 25.5&nbsp;km while the Retro has its own fix, out of NMEA one farther than 75.5&nbsp;km, and out of both one silent for 5&nbsp;s.
        The Bravo forgets an airborne aircraft after 6&nbsp;s of silence and one on the ground after 60&nbsp;s.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel panel-wide">
      <h2>Log</h2>
      <div class="bar">
        <button type="button" data-action="comparison#download">Download NDJSON</button>
        <button type="button" data-action="comparison#clear">Clear</button>
        <span class="state" data-comparison-target="logState">-</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hint">Every sentence and frame both receivers sent, one JSON line each: the time it arrived, the receiver, the raw line or frame, and what it decoded to.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
